<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Protectorate General to Pacify the East</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">668</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Andong Protectorate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> General to Pacify the East was set up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a> in 668, after the fall of Goguryeo, to rule the conquered lands of Goguryeo and Baekje. Its existence led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silla-tang-war">Silla–Tang War</a>, and in 676 the Tang moved it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>. It was later reduced in status and eventually abolished in the eighth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/protectorate-general-to-pacify-the-east.jpg" alt="Protectorate General to Pacify the East" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lệ Xuân · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tang_China_under_Emperor_Gaozong.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
